  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1259 PM MDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nDRIER THROUGH MONDAY:\n\nDrier conditions and cooler, more seasonable temperatures \nremain in place through Monday as high pressure builds over the \nGreat Basin. Enough moisture may still linger for some isolated \nshowers and storms over the higher terrain, but those chances \nare very low. \n\nPRECIPITATION CHANCES RETURN TUESDAY ONWARD:\n\nA low pressure system will move onto the Great Basin over the \nnext 24-36 hours. This shift will result in moisture-rich \nsouthwesterly flow setting up over the Intermountain West. At \nthe same time, high pressure sets up over Texas, drawing Gulf \nmoisture into the Desert Southwest. As a result, wet weather \nreturns to the forecast on Tuesday with storm coverage ebbing \nand flowing throughout the week. Multiple days of precipitation \nare likely, especially over the southern Mountains.",
